# ============================================================================
# TEMPLATE - DISABLED BY DEFAULT (D2B, B-authored)
# ============================================================================
# This is the DRY-RUN benchmark template for target_reach_random_1_3m_v0.
# The dry-run verifies TARGET GENERATION ONLY. It must not move the robot.
#
# Why it is a .template:
#   scripts/run_benchmark.py only executes configs ending in .yaml. Keeping
#   this file as .yaml.template means it cannot be run until it is deliberately
#   copied to .yaml. B does not perform that copy; it is done at the D3 gate
#   after A provides and reviews the dry-run experiment config below.
#
# What the dry-run is allowed to verify (see D2B doc §9):
#   - target generation (r, theta sampling)
#   - seed reproducibility (same seed -> same target)
#   - r / theta distribution sanity
#   - target_x / target_y computation
#   - target_in_bounds check
#   - artifact completeness
#   - summary generation
#
# What the dry-run must NOT do:
#   - publish /cmd_vel
#   - call move_for
#   - run scenario motion
#   - call restore
#   - change robot state
#
# Motion-gate safety:
#   The referenced dry-run experiment MUST be entry_type: check (not scenario),
#   and its task_name (target_reach_random_1_3m_dry_run_v0) does not contain any
#   MOTION_TASK_KEYWORDS (base_probe / base_forward / move_for / scenario), so
#   the benchmark runner's motion gate will NOT require --allow-motion. This is
#   correct: the dry-run is not motion. If the experiment ever becomes a
#   scenario or emits motion, the gate will refuse it and this template must be
#   re-reviewed.
#
# Prerequisite before enabling:
#   A must provide configs/experiments/target_reach_random_1_3m_dry_run_v0.yaml
#   (B does NOT author motion or target-generation experiment configs). Until
#   that file exists, copying this template to .yaml will make run_benchmark.py
#   fail with FileNotFoundError on the referenced experiment, which is the safe
#   failure mode.
# ============================================================================
schema_version: "0.2"
benchmark_id: target_reach_random_1_3m_dry_run_20
description: >-
  [TEMPLATE / DISABLED] Dry-run benchmark for target_reach_random_1_3m_v0.
  Verifies target generation, seed reproducibility, and artifact completeness
  with NO robot motion. Requires A to provide the dry-run experiment config.
  See docs/tasks/target_reach_random_1_3m_v0_B_benchmark_and_metrics.md §9.

# The dry-run experiment config is provided by A at the D3 gate.
# It does not exist yet; B does not create it.
experiment_configs:
  - configs/experiments/target_reach_random_1_3m_dry_run_v0.yaml

runs_per_experiment: 20
operator: B

# Episodes are launched via the standard episode runner only. The benchmark
# runner never calls PowerShell, Docker, restore, or /cmd_vel directly.
launch:
  command: "python scripts/run_episode.py --config {config} --operator {operator}"
